<!-- cell: markdown id="1bb474c2-e1e6-4730-a599-46d86404afb5" -->

# How the war begun

## High-level plot

1. Earth finds an artifact on Mars and begin excavating.

2. The artifact is actually a living organism and the excavation is damaging it. It sends a signal to its race, who come to protect it.

3. Earth sees the ships coming out of hyper-space, and thinks it's an attack. 

4. War begins.

## Low-level plot

1.1. [earth] The space agency on Earth spots an irregular shape under Mars's surface in a probe's scans, and broadcasts the finding worldwide.

1.2. [mars] Excavation team is sent, robots are lowered down and begin excavating

1.3. [mars] Excavation uncovers the object made out of rare materials, resembling a stone sculpture. 

1.4. [orbit] Samples are sent to orbit, to a laboratory ship. Scientists begin studying the object.

2.1. [mars] The object is an organism embedded in the rock. It was monitoring the probe's movement and its scan, and the arrival of the excavation team.

2.2. [mars] The excavation begins, and the organism grows concern. But it's not until the excavators pierce its exoskeleton, hurting it, that is sends a distress call.

2.3. [mars] The communication is FTL, he is asked what is the nautre of emergency. The organism says he was discovered and attacked. He is told to stay put and that help is on the way.

3.1. [orbit] Alien ships emerge on a far orbit around Mars. Earth ships spot them immediately. 

3.2. [orbit] Earth sends orders to protect the discovery. The mission consists of the lab ship and one weakly armed escort. 

3.3. [orbit] Ships are approaching, they are completely foreign and no one on the earth ships knows how to even interpret if they are powering up weapons or not. hails are sent, but to no effect.

3.4. [orbit] Scientists on the lab ship are scrambling in attempt to understand anything about the alien ships. They suspect they are here for the artifact, and they are trying to correlate what they found with the sensor readings. The mineral scans agree, the origin seems the same, but that doesn't say anything about communication.

3.5. [mars] All the while the excavation efforts are not stoping, the scientists wanting to find out more about the fleet that approaches by studying the object buried on Mars.

4.1. [mars] The object communicates with the fleet that he is in need of dire assistance.

4.2. [orbit] The fleet observes the efforts and identifies the ships in orbit, classifying them as belionging to the same tribe as the entities attacking the object.

4.3. [orbit] They fire on the ships in orbit, decimating them.

4.4. [mars] They automated excavators stop.

4.5. [earth] Earth notices the disapeparance of the ships, and assumes they have just been attacked in an act of war.

<!-- cell: plot id="eb95bb84-666a-442c-973f-8364ea6080d9" title="How the war begun (high-level)" nodes="3838abc8-e2d5-4465-ada4-0313f8faea8b:7-15, 8bacfa2c-64dd-4b0f-8f9f-03e0ed76db4b:17-41, 4c507036-d7ec-4475-8c0a-79f127995ae5:43-55, 6bffc590-9df0-436b-91c2-d813cd467b2a:57-58" edges="7f257336-180f-4415-83cd-a39c836692cc:3838abc8-e2d5-4465-ada4-0313f8faea8b>8bacfa2c-64dd-4b0f-8f9f-03e0ed76db4b, 81685398-0c74-40cf-9302-b2abc0ee5037:8bacfa2c-64dd-4b0f-8f9f-03e0ed76db4b>4c507036-d7ec-4475-8c0a-79f127995ae5, 7f6fb523-1508-477f-bdad-a9dea03c43c2:4c507036-d7ec-4475-8c0a-79f127995ae5>6bffc590-9df0-436b-91c2-d813cd467b2a" -->

How the alien race attacked Earth and why.

<!-- cell: plot id="96b07979-7be6-4ce4-a6a4-fdb269f81466" title="How the war begun (low-level)" nodes="78f58d5c-7cbf-4703-b827-ac1e99484c51:61-83, 17407ff9-1ee0-48f6-9715-975d604056a3:84-96, 981dcaa2-1eec-4154-8f4f-691a8f6331e1:97-111, 026c4034-fdcd-4e06-a98b-02e1b975f6bc:112-127, 18fa90e9-d869-4af2-96f6-671e4141a51a:128-154, 1c1b9e2c-f93d-44d7-80c3-65a252c56c43:155-181, caaf77c9-54c7-4651-b27f-7b83af728116:182-217, 85a84899-678c-4bf5-a781-3c0929af8d4f:218-233, 902418fc-9e01-4c58-ba91-4da58e89d652:234-254, 2e8b2bb3-7a25-4f36-8bef-ec34721d75d2:255-290, 715999ae-42f2-4440-bc79-7fff0e43a5a2:291-345, 5d44d092-b857-4bd9-ae54-7cada30f2265:346-375, 42ddb454-8d5c-4712-ba8b-c1189c79bbc0:376-391, 45801474-bce9-4977-8b09-04568814c95d:392-418, dd589b4e-4c7a-4f4f-a9cb-404ec06ee196:419-429, 4b149bc0-f217-4ec1-a863-78ae85da52ba:430-435, 27e2080d-a10b-4c1e-a22f-f4bb52ee34b7:436-456" edges="8c1e507b-7ce0-4319-a470-d7db8470c2ab:78f58d5c-7cbf-4703-b827-ac1e99484c51>17407ff9-1ee0-48f6-9715-975d604056a3, 86e0c370-b499-448c-b32d-cbba25ee73bf:17407ff9-1ee0-48f6-9715-975d604056a3>981dcaa2-1eec-4154-8f4f-691a8f6331e1, 068c1b1c-69c1-4f29-b25e-e8bf05869287:981dcaa2-1eec-4154-8f4f-691a8f6331e1>026c4034-fdcd-4e06-a98b-02e1b975f6bc, a0d5f4a7-6bc0-4c39-baed-c52acb26a702:18fa90e9-d869-4af2-96f6-671e4141a51a>1c1b9e2c-f93d-44d7-80c3-65a252c56c43, 645bc048-2064-4d91-964f-1287cf09cfe5:1c1b9e2c-f93d-44d7-80c3-65a252c56c43>caaf77c9-54c7-4651-b27f-7b83af728116, 43cfa2dc-1c49-4629-918c-9e6c3c4d39ca:85a84899-678c-4bf5-a781-3c0929af8d4f>902418fc-9e01-4c58-ba91-4da58e89d652, 3429c43a-2bc8-4d47-9543-4a120028fac9:902418fc-9e01-4c58-ba91-4da58e89d652>2e8b2bb3-7a25-4f36-8bef-ec34721d75d2, 1819178c-df4a-4eb6-a648-f3d093f4ae79:2e8b2bb3-7a25-4f36-8bef-ec34721d75d2>715999ae-42f2-4440-bc79-7fff0e43a5a2, 9e195f4d-061f-41d5-aa19-8a436ea47aca:715999ae-42f2-4440-bc79-7fff0e43a5a2>5d44d092-b857-4bd9-ae54-7cada30f2265, 062d2ff2-c158-4457-9e8b-82138eede9e5:42ddb454-8d5c-4712-ba8b-c1189c79bbc0>45801474-bce9-4977-8b09-04568814c95d, aef24e87-32b6-45e9-b952-5b5a3c140425:45801474-bce9-4977-8b09-04568814c95d>dd589b4e-4c7a-4f4f-a9cb-404ec06ee196, d77fec95-e699-4225-99d7-80a20b962c1a:dd589b4e-4c7a-4f4f-a9cb-404ec06ee196>4b149bc0-f217-4ec1-a863-78ae85da52ba, 848d2734-d949-4487-8221-e0f393a4f777:4b149bc0-f217-4ec1-a863-78ae85da52ba>27e2080d-a10b-4c1e-a22f-f4bb52ee34b7, ae990dc0-412d-4a61-b053-a7efedcbe994:026c4034-fdcd-4e06-a98b-02e1b975f6bc>18fa90e9-d869-4af2-96f6-671e4141a51a, baf5d260-62b0-48b8-91d6-2fc57dce264c:caaf77c9-54c7-4651-b27f-7b83af728116>85a84899-678c-4bf5-a781-3c0929af8d4f, f350041c-4bf5-4924-98dc-681e0e3f11a9:5d44d092-b857-4bd9-ae54-7cada30f2265>42ddb454-8d5c-4712-ba8b-c1189c79bbc0" -->

The discovery of an alien object on Mars. The alien object on Mars alerts its race of it being attacked and requests assistance. The alien fleet arrives at Mars to help defend their fellow. The aliens fire on the ships in Mars orbit, preventing further damage to their fellow on Mars.

<!-- cell: markdown id="1395a7f0-9154-4766-8333-681a0e2fe965" -->

# Captain Varn and her daughter

## High-level plot

1. Captain Varn leaves her daughter on Earth to command the corvette that escorts the mission to Mars.

2. At Mars, Varn and her daughter keep talking, and Varn tells her of her doubts about the excavation.

3. When the alien fleet arrives, Varn fears it will go on to Earth.

4. Varn believes her daughter will have no chance unless someone stands in the fleet's way. She says goodbye to her daughter, puts her corvette in the fleet's path, and dies.

## Low-level plot

1.1. [earth, Varn's house] Captain Varn watches the news with her daughter: a probe has found something under the surface of Mars.

1.2. [earth, command center] Varn is given command of the corvette that will escort the mission to Mars, and tells her daughter she has to leave.

1.3. [earth, Varn's house] Varn says goodbye to her daughter and promises to talk to her every day.

1.4. [orbit] Varn's corvette arrives at Mars with the laboratory ship, as the first samples come up from the excavation.

2.1. [orbit] Varn calls her daughter. Her daughter says she misses her, and Varn says she misses her too.

2.2. [orbit] Varn watches the excavators dig deeper, and tells her daughter that no one knows what the object is, yet the digging goes on.

2.3. [earth] Varn's daughter asks whether the object is dangerous, and Varn tells her not to worry.

3.1. [orbit] Varn sees alien ships appear on her corvette's screens, far out around Mars.

3.2. [orbit] Varn is ordered to protect the discovery, and knows her one weakly armed corvette cannot stop a fleet.

3.3. [orbit] Varn hails the alien ships again and again, and gets no answer.

3.4. [orbit] Varn asks the scientists on the laboratory ship what the aliens want, and they cannot tell her.

3.5. [orbit] Varn tells her daughter about the ships, and that she is afraid they will go on to Earth.

4.1. [orbit] Varn believes that unless someone stands in the fleet's way, her daughter will have no chance on Earth. She sends her daughter a last message to say goodbye.

4.2. [orbit] Varn moves her corvette into the fleet's path to buy her daughter time.

4.3. [orbit] The fleet fires, and Varn's corvette is destroyed.

4.5. [earth] Varn's daughter receives her mother's last message.

<!-- cell: plot id="dca7728d-3313-43e2-9dc1-2878b99cc3c0" title="Captain Varn and her daughter (high-level)" nodes="e424b0c8-2808-4d87-97ef-eed1b1c4a740:465-481, f614d64f-2b40-4248-8567-48efef1f5e37:483-500, b91c62c9-7fe5-43e9-9df5-129ad57da9db:502-514, 9cacf434-9ae3-4b5a-8439-9a2cce0b73ec:516-545" edges="4dff3ba5-f9d0-45ab-b6ba-b80033e2e88c:e424b0c8-2808-4d87-97ef-eed1b1c4a740>f614d64f-2b40-4248-8567-48efef1f5e37, 66dbf0c0-3005-44f7-add7-45561f9e25a1:f614d64f-2b40-4248-8567-48efef1f5e37>b91c62c9-7fe5-43e9-9df5-129ad57da9db, bf8971a3-660a-46b4-b7a9-96a9055f1821:b91c62c9-7fe5-43e9-9df5-129ad57da9db>9cacf434-9ae3-4b5a-8439-9a2cce0b73ec" -->

How Captain Varn gave her life to buy her daughter time.

<!-- cell: plot id="0ba0da30-1107-4920-9637-b37bca145789" title="Captain Varn and her daughter (low-level)" nodes="ac450db2-4e30-4b8c-a299-e0539c1c3c03:548-569, ebbc016a-d49f-45aa-831f-e7c201d7aa88:570-595, a5c674da-08a1-425f-ae73-65bf32505dd4:596-613, e238dfd0-3bbb-47a2-8bf8-21a752bc8011:614-633, 9a791f4c-d54c-48fb-8088-e963ebc5491c:634-652, ba8d58bd-bebc-4c41-9151-045bcaa70a72:653-677, 154d142c-cf04-4e91-82dc-747f85dda7f5:678-694, 7ed2958a-b4ef-485d-b6fd-8255e0c48205:695-709, 8487e6b3-9c20-42c7-8870-30d14c184033:710-729, 2ef7ac99-d328-497e-96ce-e24d6f241b41:730-743, 49c17798-07f4-48b0-a4c0-9af31d6834a4:744-762, cbf88628-c1dd-46bf-8f11-0efe989a85eb:763-782, cd191fae-6fab-4947-8e0b-2151da3c3de6:783-812, c77e468d-2b09-4523-b12d-73afd2ff8acc:813-827, a87ad0c3-efc8-49c8-a44e-6fb6735835a2:828-837, 5bb2c34b-d3e7-468e-bded-bd4a7dfed052:838-846" edges="be9f3907-80db-4266-aeab-13658c114004:ac450db2-4e30-4b8c-a299-e0539c1c3c03>ebbc016a-d49f-45aa-831f-e7c201d7aa88, 680cb49c-61ec-493c-b7b5-b0f7ae98966d:ebbc016a-d49f-45aa-831f-e7c201d7aa88>a5c674da-08a1-425f-ae73-65bf32505dd4, e3150870-e21b-437c-b2fb-3ab3cc490da3:a5c674da-08a1-425f-ae73-65bf32505dd4>e238dfd0-3bbb-47a2-8bf8-21a752bc8011, 0ec1d0f9-3e65-4dff-aa9a-37705671ef4a:e238dfd0-3bbb-47a2-8bf8-21a752bc8011>9a791f4c-d54c-48fb-8088-e963ebc5491c, 349dabc1-77c0-449a-9e5e-911211da5275:9a791f4c-d54c-48fb-8088-e963ebc5491c>ba8d58bd-bebc-4c41-9151-045bcaa70a72, ed793d2c-da3b-4c3d-9a84-8589b810cdb3:ba8d58bd-bebc-4c41-9151-045bcaa70a72>154d142c-cf04-4e91-82dc-747f85dda7f5, fe5e35f6-7834-45d5-8f7d-9b6aaba94004:154d142c-cf04-4e91-82dc-747f85dda7f5>7ed2958a-b4ef-485d-b6fd-8255e0c48205, de9fc47e-0ec5-4f0e-aa5d-860d0a8c1f5c:7ed2958a-b4ef-485d-b6fd-8255e0c48205>8487e6b3-9c20-42c7-8870-30d14c184033, e94e87ee-f5ee-44e2-976c-6812dcb6e900:8487e6b3-9c20-42c7-8870-30d14c184033>2ef7ac99-d328-497e-96ce-e24d6f241b41, a972c2b1-bbae-42d9-bd35-bb2c055f228a:2ef7ac99-d328-497e-96ce-e24d6f241b41>49c17798-07f4-48b0-a4c0-9af31d6834a4, 26909aba-22e1-4369-b492-02c3d9b1a947:49c17798-07f4-48b0-a4c0-9af31d6834a4>cbf88628-c1dd-46bf-8f11-0efe989a85eb, 8a3009bc-03b8-420c-b153-83549cb831a3:cbf88628-c1dd-46bf-8f11-0efe989a85eb>cd191fae-6fab-4947-8e0b-2151da3c3de6, 557b09dd-bb68-47f2-9735-d514f01c7d81:cd191fae-6fab-4947-8e0b-2151da3c3de6>c77e468d-2b09-4523-b12d-73afd2ff8acc, 503fbf1d-dbc3-483a-b1e8-8d59845b525b:c77e468d-2b09-4523-b12d-73afd2ff8acc>a87ad0c3-efc8-49c8-a44e-6fb6735835a2, dafc956e-ebbe-4420-827a-0586753e8e49:a87ad0c3-efc8-49c8-a44e-6fb6735835a2>5bb2c34b-d3e7-468e-bded-bd4a7dfed052" -->

Captain Varn leaves her daughter to escort the mission to Mars, keeps talking to her, and dies standing in the alien fleet's way.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="8e8a6674-478c-419d-896c-90a260f85822" title="The traveller" words="050b7c47-f1d5-4cc9-be63-4f6dc4483660:17-29, 8a55b6b4-4676-4603-9027-9bd910fa6191:130-154, 3879704f-4731-49d0-9f0e-f680a210613e:157-181, 35e606b6-0b30-45aa-9de4-0e05d32a8cb5:197-204" -->

A lone alien stranded on Mars after a crash, who only wants to survive until its people come for it. Hurt by beings it cannot understand, it calls for help.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="5f9cd3d4-c51b-4dc6-bdc7-776861df77da" title="The alien race" words="07d7df7a-142f-49bd-8b74-195d2cf2156d:30-41, 4cbe19e8-cad8-480e-a0c8-9fed365054c5:205-217, b04e6690-be33-4edc-9167-3f4f88de4afc:394-418, ca4dd131-6d60-4eb5-94e6-66a6b74930bd:421-429" -->

A people who come for one of their own, and treat whoever is hurting it as the enemy.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="c1bf1836-9a18-4db7-8df5-798d9b55fb73" title="Humanity" words="803e7f0f-3f7d-400b-8d23-a7ad1ee72e84:7-15, 0085edeb-7752-4c6a-89a8-97c8e0b69bb1:99-111, 931f009e-f61c-4da1-8a3c-cf27c0c4508e:114-127, a9fe2a9f-ea80-415c-8288-b465ac70392e:236-242, 17eaf369-53a9-40bc-9979-329c1dc15d35:348-375, e9a97711-44b1-4bc8-afbd-96ebbd53ee58:438-456" -->

The side that hurts a living being without knowing it is alive, and then takes its people's arrival and strike for an attack.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="832fea15-0d66-42e4-9299-35ef692642ee" title="The faster-than-light link" words="569dda37-7121-4712-9a0d-458a9673949a:184-196, a9f49cfd-bd85-4b39-b31f-bb5fecbac173:378-391" -->

The traveller's only way to reach its people. Through it a stranding becomes a rescue, and an injury becomes a call to war.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="581dedf1-c744-401f-85cb-26bc4bcb5532" title="Misunderstanding" words="740df94b-2aae-4663-9ba2-ff2792d8e26d:43-55, fdb3c91d-d018-4dc4-ab55-205746aecc8b:257-290, 8ff4d31c-27b8-4c48-91a9-97855bc1f273:330-345, 49537012-4c24-49f4-8f84-9e951585e187:405-418, 3f9ba1f4-9b3d-4f20-bc87-4f1c3b317dd1:446-456" -->

Neither side can read the other, so each takes the other's actions for an attack.

<!-- cell: salient-concept id="2d8238ef-1765-48e7-b778-8d463b3d27df" title="War" words="d6c12376-13d3-4f79-9051-b363f68cf421:57-58, e0bef313-726c-4e9d-9674-1e23498ef86f:421-429, be31be95-c2dd-4501-b60e-a996d264d128:451-456" -->

How a war begins that no one meant to start.
